{"id":77,"flavor":[{"games":["Legends: Arceus"],"text":"These Pokémon live in herds out in the grassland. Newborn foals lack their fiery manes, which will develop about an hour after birth."},{"games":["Shield"],"text":"If you’ve been accepted by Ponyta, its burning mane is mysteriously no longer hot to the touch."},{"games":["Sword"],"text":"It can’t run properly when it’s newly born. As it races around with others of its kind, its legs grow stronger."},{"games":["Let’s Go, Eevee!","Let’s Go, Pikachu!","Yellow"],"text":"Capable of jumping incredibly high. Its hooves and sturdy legs absorb the impact of a hard landing."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Omega Ruby","Sapphire","Ruby"],"text":"Ponyta is very weak at birth. It can barely stand up. This Pokémon becomes stronger by stumbling and falling to keep up with its parent."},{"games":["Y","Pearl"],"text":"Its legs grow strong while it chases after its parent. It runs in fields and mountains all day."},{"games":["X","White 2","Black 2","White","Black","Platinum"],"text":"As a newborn, it can barely stand. However, through galloping, its legs are made tougher and faster."},{"games":["SoulSilver"],"text":"Its hind legs, which have hooves that are harder than diamond, kick back at any presence it senses behind it."},{"games":["HeartGold","Gold"],"text":"It is a weak runner immediately after birth. It gradually becomes faster by chasing after its parents."},{"games":["Diamond"],"text":"About an hour after birth, its fiery mane and tail grow out, giving it an impressive appearance."},{"games":["LeafGreen"],"text":"Its hooves are ten times harder than diamond. It can trample anything completely flat in little time."},{"games":["FireRed"],"text":"Its body is light, and its legs are incredibly powerful. It can clear Ayers Rock in one leap."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"A PONYTA is very weak at birth. It can barely stand up. Its legs become stronger as it stumbles and falls while trying to keep up with its parent."},{"games":[